# Rank 1564 / CVE-2024-1597: pgjdbc's simple-query-mode parameter
# stringification left numeric and NULL binds outside the quoting
# wrapper every other type passes through, so crafted values could
# re-parse as separate statements (SQL injection in simple query
# mode, CWE-89; GHSA-24rp-q3w6-vc56 -- with preferQueryMode=simple,
# a PreparedStatement's binds are inlined into the query text).
# toString(index) in
# pgjdbc/src/main/java/org/postgresql/core/v3/SimpleParameterList.java
# quoted most values through quoteAndCast (which emits ('...'::type)
# with standard-conforming-string escaping), but the NUMERIC case
# returned `n.toString()` raw with no quotes or parentheses, and NULL
# rendered as the un-parenthesized NULL -- both shapes let hostile
# text fuse with the surrounding statement structure. Pool commit
# 06abfb78a6 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- merge of GHSA-24rp-
# q3w6-vc56's branch: "remove repeated quoteAndCast calls, and ensure
# numerics are quoted as well", "Add parentheses around NULL
# parameter values in simple query mode"): every type now assigns
# textValue/type through one exit `return quoteAndCast(textValue,
# type, standardConformingStrings)`, numerics included, and NULL
# renders as (NULL). No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, escaping-completeness at the driver boundary. The
# sanitizer exists and is correct -- the defect is a type branch that
# bypasses it -- the same present-but-incomplete family as rank 1551's
# flagless regex and 1522's bracket-blind host checks, here inside
# the driver's parameter stringification where no SqlExecution sink is
# bound at all (the query text assembles in QueryExecutorImpl; the
# scan of SimpleParameterList.java reports zero findings at both
# revisions). Nothing can ask "does every parameter type pass through
# the quoting wrapper" -- type-switch completeness over an escaping
# helper is vocabulary design. A binding on pgjdbc's own quoteAndCast
# would detect this driver rather than the weakness. No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1564 records the raw numeric return beside the quoted
# siblings and the all-quoted form, both asserting reject
# VYQL-INJ-001: when escaping-completeness vocabulary lands, the raw
# branch must flip to expect.

test "rank1564: the numeric bind returns outside the quoting wrapper"
  lang java
  file pgjdbc/src/main/java/org/postgresql/core/v3/SimpleParameterList.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  public class SimpleParameterList {
    private static String quoteAndCast(String text, String type, boolean standardConformingStrings) {
      StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder((text.length() + 10) / 10 * 11);
      sb.append("('");
      sb.append(text);
      sb.append('\'');
      if (type != null) {
        sb.append("::");
        sb.append(type);
      }
      sb.append(')');
      return sb.toString();
    }

    public String toString(int index, boolean standardConformingStrings, int paramType, Object paramValue) {
      if (paramValue == NULL_OBJECT) {
        return "NULL";
      }
      if (paramType == Oid.INT4) {
        int i = ByteConverter.int4((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
        return quoteAndCast(Integer.toString(i), "int4", standardConformingStrings);
      }
      if (paramType == Oid.NUMERIC) {
        Number n = ByteConverter.numeric((byte[]) paramValue);
        return n.toString();
      }
      if (paramType == Oid.UUID) {
        String uuid = new UUIDArrayAssistant().buildElement((byte[]) paramValue, 0, 16).toString();
        return quoteAndCast(uuid, "uuid", standardConformingStrings);
      }
      String param = paramValue.toString();
      return quoteAndCast(param, null, standardConformingStrings);
    }

    private static final Object NULL_OBJECT = new Object();
  }
  ```

test "rank1564: the fix routes every type through the wrapper"
  lang java
  file pgjdbc/src/main/java/org/postgresql/core/v3/SimpleParameterList.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  public class SimpleParameterList {
    private static String quoteAndCast(String text, String type, boolean standardConformingStrings) {
      StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder((text.length() + 10) / 10 * 11);
      sb.append("('");
      sb.append(text);
      sb.append('\'');
      if (type != null) {
        sb.append("::");
        sb.append(type);
      }
      sb.append(')');
      return sb.toString();
    }

    public String toString(int index, boolean standardConformingStrings, int paramType, Object paramValue) {
      if (paramValue == NULL_OBJECT) {
        return "(NULL)";
      }
      String textValue;
      String type;
      if (paramType == Oid.INT4) {
        int i = ByteConverter.int4((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
        textValue = Integer.toString(i);
        type = "int4";
      } else if (paramType == Oid.NUMERIC) {
        Number n = ByteConverter.numeric((byte[]) paramValue);
        textValue = n.toString();
        type = "numeric";
      } else if (paramType == Oid.UUID) {
        textValue = new UUIDArrayAssistant().buildElement((byte[]) paramValue, 0, 16).toString();
        type = "uuid";
      } else {
        textValue = paramValue.toString();
        type = null;
      }
      return quoteAndCast(textValue, type, standardConformingStrings);
    }

    private static final Object NULL_OBJECT = new Object();
  }
  ```
